  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe first slice of the Rotary Flow kind (issue #2824, part of #2804): a 4-axis cylindrical flow-line kernel in `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/`, split over four files under the 400-line law.\n\n- `rotary_flow.rs` - the public entry. `rotary_flow(chains, facets, ax, p, c)` takes the picked guide chains, the part facets, the STATED rotation axis (the #2772 seam - the axis is a parameter, never fitted here), `RotaryFlowParams` and `AxisControl`. The params carry the `Tool` itself, so the ball-nose requirement is refused by name. Clearance and retract read as ball-center radii about the axis.\n- `rotary_flow_unwrap.rs` - each chain unwound to a continuous `(theta, v)` track (the radian twin of `cl::unwrap_near`), each adjacent pair aligned by the nearest whole turn, the band developed `(s = R_ref * theta, v)` with `R_ref` the chains' outermost radius, and the picked-chain ground checks (finite, distinct, on-model, off-axis).\n- `rotary_flow_pass.rs` - the iso-parametric flow curves between the aligned pair, each station's ball center pushed out along its radial until the `closest_pt_tri` oracle clears every facet (march, then bisect), the curve chorded within `min(ARC_FIT_TOL, tolerance)` over the union of the two chains' arc-length knots.\n- `rotary_flow_emit.rs` - tips via the pivot law (`retip`), cut poses through the lean law on the radial (`tilt`), links rebuilt radially on the retract cylinders (`rotary_links`' law: feed retract, chorded index short way round, radial plunge), the program opening on the clearance pose (M13.8).\n\nRefusals by name: a tool that is not a ball-nose, fewer than two chains, a non-finite point, a point off the model, a point on the axis line, chains wound in opposite senses, a band with no width, a stepover or tolerance at the scallop ceiling (the finishing kinds' own law), a station the push-out cannot clear within five radii, a pass count over the 4096-pass ceiling, a clearance that does not clear the work.\n\nThe decisions taken unattended are in `docs/decisions/2824-rotary-flow-kernel.md`: the `Tool`-carrying params (the drilling precedent), the ball-center radius reading of the heights, `R_ref` at the chains' outermost radius (ground inside it gets finer, never coarser), and one band per adjacent chain pair with both edge passes kept (a shared middle chain is walked once per band - the re-cut is the same geometry at the same depth).\n\n## The readings\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 29 steps, 0 failed - motion lib, `multiaxis`, `rotary`, the new `rotary_flow` binary, and the reached app suites (operations, posed_contact, rotary_fixtures, rotary_verify, and the rest). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n- On the rotor groove fixture: the developed band reads 4.000 mm at R 8.000 mm; 6 flow passes at a 0.9 mm stepover; the first pass rides the wall push-out (rho about 11), interior passes ride the floor a ball radius off it; every cut station's ball keeps its radius off the part.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary_flow/rotary_flow_tests.rs` (15 tests): every refusal by name (non-ball tool, chain count, empty model, off-model at its spot, on-axis, degenerate band, opposite senses, both scallop ceilings, low clearance), the pass count law, `align_pair`'s nearest whole turn, `lerp_at`, `unwrap_near`, and a small on-model band that poses, clears and opens at clearance.\n- `crates/motion/tests/rotary_flow.rs` (3 run, 1 heavy): `a_rotor_floor_band_flows_multi_turn_without_gouge` (the no-gouge pin over every station against `camcraft_sim`'s own `dist_seg_tri`, multi-turn span, wall vs floor riders), `a_pair_straddling_the_branch_aligns_by_a_whole_turn` (same pass count as the unshifted band, the note stating the shift), `climb_reverses_each_pass`, and the ignored `the_rotor_envelope_stays_gouge_free_at_the_scallop_law` (heavy lane: release --ignored, the 4-turn fine rotor envelope scanned station by station).\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The app layer, the command and the MCP tool are owed to the #2804 sub-issues; this PR changes only the motion kernel.\n- The whole-turn alignment is pinned by the kernel basis' own branch (e1 = +Y on a Z axis); a pair straddling a different frame's branch reaches the same law through the same shift.\n- A band whose pair meets at a whole-turn boundary exactly (offset = half a lap) is not tested; the nearest-turn law would pick either side.\n- `graphify update` did not run: the `graphify` command is not on this session's PATH.\n- Heavy lane: only the ignored envelope scan touches it; it runs at the cut.\n\nChangelog: multiaxis: Rotary Flow - a 4-axis flow-line finishing kernel between picked helical guide chains on a stated rotation axis\n\nfork synced at v0.25.0\n\nPart of #2804. `Refs #2824`, not `Fixes`: the umbrella issue's Done means spans all its sub-issues, so the sub-issue closes with its siblings, not here.\n\nRefs #2824\n",
